From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:09:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 087/148] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on the rail's
 open-in-every-session setting: start a restored panel closed instead of
 closing it

The rail no longer claims the room until the user's first click: that blocked keyboard users, closed panels the agent opened while the user typed, reopened the rail when a new chat's temp id became real, and closed panels through the header toggle, which saved the close as the user's choice and the app-wide default. Now AppShell's two workspace-panel restores pass through aeRailRestoredPanelOpen (lib/aeSessionRail.ts): with the setting on, on a desktop, with no file or comment in the URL, a restored panel that would not fit beside the rail starts closed for this view, and nothing is saved. On a session switch the rail opens; a new chat's id swap is not a switch. Every later panel open swaps with the rail as before.

Settings > Chat now sits in SettingsPage's own Section shell (exporting Section would have made an import cycle), and its nav icon has its own file. test-setup.ts keeps the setting off by default, in the store and in storage, because upstream's shell tests do not mock the rail's sections; the rail's tests, including a new AppShell-level one, turn it on.
